**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Campaign artifacts are fetched from the Zenodo deposit or regenerated on a
# GPU; they are not source. Target FASTA and structures under data/targets are
# tracked, because they are small and are inputs rather than outputs.
# Per-campaign composition tables are a few kB and are what the notebook
# reads, so they are tracked. The per-step loss log is the subject of the
# steering analysis and is tracked too, at roughly 450 kB per campaign for
# 30 seeds by 150 steps. Full results tables and predicted structures are
# large and stay in the deposit.
data/campaigns/*
!data/campaigns/.gitkeep
!data/campaigns/*/
data/campaigns/*/*
!data/campaigns/*/composition.parquet
!data/campaigns/*/protocol.json
!data/campaigns/*/step_trace.parquet
# The per-design results table is 32 kB and carries the designed sequences,
# which are the most reusable output here, so it is tracked. Its CSV twin is
# not: same content, and nothing reads it. The predicted structures are 5 MB
# per campaign and stay in the deposit; nothing in the notebook reads them,
# because composition is measured once at collection time.
!data/campaigns/*/all_results.parquet
data/derived/*
!data/derived/.gitkeep
# The composition table and the query record are small and are the inputs the
# notebook needs, so they are tracked and the pub renders from a fresh clone
# with no deposit. The 4 MB per-entity pairs table stays deposit-only.
# Nothing here is tracked. The reference set is derived from a recorded RCSB
# query and public coordinates, so a reader reproduces it rather than receiving
# it: analysis.rcsb.build runs when the table is absent. Shipping it would mean
# shipping something the notebook can and should derive.
data/reference/*
!data/reference/.gitkeep

# Jupyter real-time-collaboration state, written by the server when a client
# opens a notebook. Local session bookkeeping, not a project artifact.
.jupyter/
.jupyter_ystore.db
